  "source_streaming_state": {
    "conv1d": "conv.py:239-275 uses effective_kernel=(kernel-1)*dilation+1, total causal left pad=effective_kernel-stride once per fresh stream, constant-zero mode. streaming.py:465-511 caches previous raw input, concatenates on next call, computes only full windows, and retains input from num_frames*stride onward. For all decoder Conv1d stride1, k7 history6, k3 history2, k1 history0.",
    "convtranspose1d": "streaming.py:514-570 initial partial=None, reset->None. Each call computes full raw ConvTranspose1d, adds saved partial to the first K-S samples with `partial - bias` when bias is present, saves the new last K-S output samples as partial, and emits the prefix. Decoder four stages have K-S=8,6,5,4 and bias=True. conv.py:334-344 outer causal trim_right_ratio=1.0 trims all K-S on the right only when not streaming; no outer trim in streaming mode.",
    "reset": "server.py:115-117 starts streaming_forever(1); server.py:263-267 resets both Mimi stream states at a new chat. A standalone native reference should use one decoder.streaming(1) context for consecutive frames and fresh/reset state for replay.",
    "residual_add": "streaming.py:434-461 StreamingAdd buffers unmatched shortcut/branch tails, adds only min available length, and resets both previous_x/previous_y to None."
  },
